now our dw investigative team has been  working with the china science  investigation that's a european  journalistic research project which is  led by the dutch platform follow the  money and a german non-profit newsroom  corrective  for several months 11 investigative  desks in seven countries have been  probing the nature of collaborations  between chinese and european scientists  now the team reveals that a lot of the  joint research has direct links to the  chinese military  this is a promotional video for one of  china's top universities  [Music]  the videos for the national university  of defense technology or nudt  the place that's deeply integrated with  the chinese military  it's all part of what's called military  civil fusion  as practiced by china's ruling communist  party  military civil fusion or mcf is  enormously important because it  essentially inserts the military into  all aspects of the economy  and vice versa okay so why are we  talking about this well the nudt and  other chinese universities like it have  been getting help in their mission  from right here in europe  dw and its partners in the china science  investigation have been investigating  links between these institutions and  european universities  and we've discovered a huge array of  connections  including almost 3 000 scientific  publications co-authored by both sides  someone highly sensitive subject  german researchers have worked on more  than 230 papers with the nudt  so this is a big trove of papers we  looked at a lot of them and a lot of  them seem quite innocuous but we also  found some papers that might have a dual  use application so that means they could  be used for civilian but also for  military purposes one quite interesting  example is a study that looks at how you  can track groups of people and china of  course is a surveillance state that  might have an interest in tracking for  example a certain ethnic group like the  uyghurs so you can see this is an  interesting example that could have  civilian but also more nefarious  military applications  research on dual use technologies is  meant to be carefully regulated so we  talk to the head of one major funding  body  [Music]  our team took a closer look at dozens of  individual scientists who came from  china to germany to work on advanced  projects  we're not identifying them  [Music]  scientist a is a particle physicist she  spent two years at a nuclear physics  institute in italy  and a further three at universities in  hamburg and mainz in germany  now she's back in china at the china  academy of engineering physics  as the ca ep's website vividly shows  it's china's research facility dedicated  to nuclear weapons  scientist b is a chemist who spent three  years at advanced research institutes in  berlin  before moving for a further year to  liverpool in the uk  now he's a member of the central  military commission led by president xi  jinping  that's china's highest defense body  [Music]  scientist c is an expert in hypersonic  flight who conducted doctoral research  at munich's technical university he now  leads multiple research projects funded  by china's central military commission  including two described as important  national defense projects  several of the scientists we looked at  were in germany thanks to the  government-backed humboldt foundation  its secretary general told us what he's  trying to achieve  we need to build trust  if an autocratic regime goes wild that  cannot be prevented but what we can do  is we can push  the limit where  competition  turns toward physical aggression further  and further away and this i think is  what we achieve by building trust in  this global network of the humboldt  foundation  and yet as our investigation shows  questionable research projects have been  happening  so we asked the junior minister  responsible  why the government isn't preventing this  he pointed to germany's constitution  ourselves  central australia now