ging and reading and writing  and receiving encrypted messages  many virtual meetings via secure lines  obviously because we were 30 in seven  countries so there's always a risk that  something spills and now a little bit  about the methodology and we had an  original data set of roughly three  thousand uh three hundred 000 to be  specific papers  of at least one chinese scientist and  one european scientist of course that's  massive so we needed to narrow that down  which we did so we looked at only those  chinese scientists being affiliated with  defense universities or institutes  affiliated to the people's liberation  army still too much nearly three  thousand so that we narrowed further  down  to those papers where we could find a  clear line to the national university of  defense technology that's the prime  academy of the people's liberation army  and i'm afraid to say here in germany  alone we found more than 230 which we  looked into is that right now you also  looked at individual scientists from  china didn't you can can you tell us a  little bit about your findings yeah we  have been searching the met massively  also extensively in china and we were  looking for chinese scientists from  strategically important areas like  artificial intelligence physics  chemistry quantum science who had spent  at least three years in germany in the  past decade and who were then brought  back to china by the so-called 1000  talent program that is  the best known government grant program  in china and we found 80 and analyzed 26  of these 80 in particular  and quite strikingly we found 12 of  those had received a fellowship by  germany's humboldt foundation which is  government funded after all  and  while we were conducting the research  two of them  obviously noticing something  changed their cvs that we could see  online and taking off all military  references and i find that quite telling  fascinating stuff sandra peterson head  of dw's investigative team thanks so  